// worldwide (the default): about 150 games at venues on every continent, in a mix of Upcoming,
// Live and Final. For the globe as a whole: pins everywhere, clusters, every status.
// The games play like real games: they score, start and finish, and a finished game soon drops out
// and a new one takes its place.
// Raptors v Celtics is written out: a close NBA game late in the 4th quarter, coming into clutch time,
// so its score pulses start once 5 minutes are left (if the score stays within 5 points).
// One game in each other sport is written out to become a Hot game, and stop being one, for the flames:
// Chiefs v Bills (4th quarter's last 4 minutes), Oilers v Flames (3rd period's last 5), Arsenal v Chelsea
// (from the 85th minute), Yankees v Red Sox (the top of the 9th, until its break), Mumbai v Chennai
// (an IPL chase into its last 2 overs) and Ireland v France (Six Nations, from the 75th minute). Each
// finishes, if the gap doesn't open first.
// Sinner v Alcaraz is written out with its sets, a set up in the 2nd, so tennis's set scores can be checked.
